Sval: Keep ImageBridge canvases updating while a texture is pending

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2093091 (mozilla-central af13fcc7d2f0,
5b40e4921d04, df7c14f5e7f5, Firefox 162). It needs the Bug 2093090
backport applied first. Adapted to ESR 153: RemoteTextureMap.cpp uses
MakeUnique where mozilla-central uses std::make_unique, and ESR lacks
Bug 2045240's aCalledInCallback parameter of
WebRenderImageHost::UseRemoteTexture, so the new
WaitForPendingRemoteTexture calls UseRemoteTexture() without it. The
logic is otherwise unchanged.

SuppressRemoteTextureReadyCheck dropped every pending ready check for
an unregistered owner, including those of unrelated image hosts. Those
hosts were never called back, kept mWaitingReadyCallback set and
ignored every later texture, so OffscreenCanvas and WebGPU canvases
presented through ImageBridge stopped updating. CancelRemoteTextureReadyCheck
cancels only the caller's own checks. WebRenderImageHost tracks its
pending check by generation and cancels it whenever its pending
textures are cleared. RecvGetSnapshot waits for pending async remote
textures, so compositor snapshots show the latest frame.

